From fec9712e1e90ae9af0d88e37866e0dbeb4439796 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:42:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(chat): flatten the session sidebar to pinned and recent

Session categories no longer split the sidebar into per-category sections.
The sidebar keeps only the pinned group and one recent group, so a session
appears once even when it belongs to a category. Category management
(rename/delete) moves to the session list actions menu, and the category
stays visible as the subtitle tag on each row.

The recent group now pages: recentCount is the page size and a "load more"
row appends older sessions instead of leaving them unreachable.

The category tag may use the full subtitle row width; the subtitle row holds
nothing else, so the previous 45% cap only truncated long category names.
